A couple of comments on the status of this:

1. Since disabled (but still physically connected monitors, like laptop's) monitors are not removed from the vector structures, this now re-enables automatically laptop's screen when there's no other backup monitor;
   - this means that laptops never go into unsafe states;
   - a new check should actually be inserted, to first use enabled monitors as backup, and disabled as last resort (I'll do this the moment Vaxry agrees with the changes);
 3. several small changes were made in order to deal with this. In general, I believe it would be better if the code now considered the possibility of a disabled (but not physically detached monitor): i.e., dealing better with monitor re-enabling (and with monitors present in the vector structures, that are actually disabled);
 4. regarding the new changes to the headless backup monitor...that breaks compatibility with other wl-roots tools that manage monitors, so if possible I would go back to the previous behaviour (I know this sucks as a proposal).

What are your feelings about this @vaxerski ?
